  "headline": "The Birthplace of Lord Rama",
  "short_description": "Ayodhya, on the banks of the Sarayu river, is revered as the birthplace of Lord Rama and a major centre of Hindu pilgrimage.",
  "about": "One of Hinduism's seven most sacred cities (Sapta Puri), Ayodhya is central to the Ramayana and has seen major temple development in recent years, including the Ram Mandir.\n\nLocated on the banks of the Sarayu river in eastern Uttar Pradesh.\n\nCentred around Ramayana-linked ritual, recitation and pilgrimage traditions, with a growing pilgrimage infrastructure.\n\nOne of Hinduism's holiest cities, sacred as the birthplace of Lord Rama.",
  "history": "An ancient city referenced extensively in the Ramayana as the capital of the Kosala kingdom under King Dasharatha and his son, Lord Rama.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Maharishi Valmiki International Airport (airport)\n- Ayodhya Dham Junction (railway)\n- Ayodhya Bus Stand (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, Awadhi, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "1–2 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Maharishi Valmiki International Airport, Ayodhya (AYJ)",
  "nearest_railway_station": "Ayodhya Dham Junction",
